# A list element is one atom, and the checker says so for a named function
# written bare in a list. It did not say so for `if`: `[if b "x" "y"]` was
# four elements on the interpreter, `<fn> true "x" "y"`, and a refusal with
# no file or line natively. `if` takes three, so the bare form is refused
# with the same message and both readings keep their spelling.
fn pick b
  [if b "x" "y"]

pub play = print (pick true)
